From e4ae1e987963e3538252a4b8cd7649f85e177789 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: proshiv85-byte <proshiv85@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:47:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 51/51] WIP: mm: memfd: answer the ashmem ioctls on memfd files

For running Android userspace on this kernel: Android's libcutils only
uses memfd for shared memory when the kernel answers the old ashmem
ioctls on memfds, otherwise it falls back to /dev/ashmem, which mainline
no longer has. Behind CONFIG_MEMFD_ASHMEM_SHIM (Android test kernel
only): size, name, protection mask (mapped onto write seals), pinning as
a no-op. Not compatible with CONFIG_DEBUG_VM (see the comment).

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic)
